            <ArticleTitle>Bypassing IgE and targeting T cells for specific immunotherapy of allergy.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>175-8</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Specific immunotherapy (SIT) is a common treatment for allergic diseases. Despite its usage in clinical practice for nearly a century, more-rational and safer allergen preparations are required. Here, the underlying mechanisms and principles of allergen modification for the future use of SIT in the treatment of allergy are discussed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
